>> title: French Toast
>> category: Flatbreads & Pancakes
>> tags: eggs, bread, breakfast, griddle, custard
>> counters: Diner
>> aka: french toast, eggy bread, pain perdu, gypsy toast
>> pairs-with: buttermilk-pancakes
>> servings: 4
>> time: 30 min
>> step.1: whisk the custard smooth
>> step.2: soak 2 min a side, no longer
>> step.3: griddle 3 min, flip, 2 min
>> step.4: pour over at the table

Whisk @eggs{4%large}(200 g), @whole milk{1%cup}(240 mL), @granulated sugar{2%Tbs}(25 g), @vanilla extract{2%tsp}(10 mL), @ground cinnamon{1/2%tsp}(1 g) and @fine sea salt{1/4%tsp} together in a wide shallow dish until no ribbons of white are left.

Soak @day-old challah{8%slices}(3/4-in thick) in @&(~1)custard{} ~soak{2%min}, turning once.

Griddle @&(~1)soaked bread{} in @unsalted butter{3%Tbs}(45 g) over medium heat ~fry{3%min}, then flip once and ~fry{2%min}, until both faces are brown and the middle has set rather than gone rubbery.

Pour @warm maple syrup{1/2%cup}(120 mL) over @&(~1)french toast{} and dust it with @confectioners sugar{1%Tbs}(8 g).
